The build/run helper is adapted from the reference's Apache-2.0 development
script. It remains Apache-2.0, separate from the GPL application.
Qt and CXX-Qt dependencies retain their own licenses. This development shell
is not a redistributable Qt SDK bundle or an installed release package.

The DPD input adapter uses PNM Viewer Toolkit's Apache-2.0 Rust decoder, pnm 0.3.6,
fetched by Cargo from https://github.com/PyPNMApps/PNM-Viewer-Toolkit.git at
5fbd5561f3e06b73486546b5ffa520279080a5eb. No decoder source is vendored here.
Cargo retains source in its ignored development cache; runtime needs no checkout.
Preserved decoder LICENSE/NOTICE are under third-party/. Resource licenses/notices
remain in the pinned upstream source and must accompany future redistributions.
The sanitized modulation-profile demo is derived from PyPNM fixtures; see
examples/measurements/single-channel/provenance.json and the applicable LICENSE/NOTICE files beside it.
PyPNM - Proactive Network Maintenance Toolkit

The shared measurement tree and Canvas patterns are adapted from
apps/qt/qml/RxMerCollectionTree.qml and RxMerBitLoadingChart.qml in the same
pinned viewer revision. Their GPL copyright notices remain in the adapted files.
The same Apache-2.0 pnm dependency decodes RxMER and channel-response files.
No network services, Python processing or viewer runtime is used.

The modulation-profile viewer adapts ModulationControls.qml, MeasurementToggle.qml,
ProfileBandwidth.qml and MeasurementChart.qml from apps/qt/qml in the same
pinned reference revision. GPL copyrights are preserved. MERLIN supplies its
own bounded adapter and uses shared Rust Shannon math on validated profiles.

The Ubuntu automatic updater adapts the staging, hash verification and privilege
boundaries of PNM Viewer Toolkit apps/viewer/src/updates/ubuntu/{download,install}.rs
(GPL-3.0-only), inspected from the local reference tree on 2026-11-11.
Copyright 2026 PNM Viewer contributors; original notices are retained.
